  booktitle={2025 International Conference on Intelligent and Secure Engineering Solutions (CISES)}, 
  title={Digital Twin-Driven Predictive Maintenance Using ML Models in Industry 5.0 Environments}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1445-1449},
  abstract={The Industry 5.0 has integrated into a new paradigm of manufacturing and industry system and the ideal convergence of man and machine. In this regard, predictive maintenance (PdM) is becoming more and more applicable, especially when it is supported by digital twins (DTs) and machine learning (ML). Digital twins are computerized representations of real equipment, and they make it easier to model and monitor quickly and diagnostics. Together with the ML models, DTs contribute to smart analysis of operational data, predicting potential failure and informing the proactive intervention minimizing non-availability and maintenance costs. The paper has presented a full-fledged analysis of the predictive maintenance as a DT-inspired approach through the ML models in Industry 5.0. It investigates the architectural, deployment and realization plan of the innovative maintenance systems which respond to the aims of the operational efficiency, organizational or technological integration as well as human centered innovation. The paper presents the theoretical foundation and the technical framework of digital twins in smart industry sensors, Internet of Things, cloud-edge infrastructures, and data fusion techniques, beforehand. It is followed by a multi-level digital twin design that has the capability of continually collecting data, offering real-time analytics and creating feedback to aid in prognosis choices regarding predictive maintenance.},
  keywords={Industries;Analytical models;Predictive models;Digital twins;Maintenance;Fifth Industrial Revolution;Sustainable development;Predictive maintenance;Smart manufacturing;Industrial Internet of Things;Digital Twin;Predictive Maintenance;Machine Learning;Industry 5.0;Smart Manufacturing;Human-in-the-Loop;Industrial IoT;Proactive Maintenance},
