  pages={348-353},
  abstract={In the changing landscape of Industry 5.0, organizational sustainability has become a strategic priority, blending technological progress with human-centered values. This paper provides theoretical insights into managing organizational sustainability, focusing on its conceptual basis and relevance within Industry 5.0. Drawing on interdisciplinary literature, the study examines key aspects such as sustainable development, organizational performance, and the integration of ethical and resilient practices. The research highlights the importance of rethinking traditional management methods to align with Industry $\mathbf{5. 0}$ principles, which emphasize collaboration between humans and intelligent systems. By discussing current trends, challenges, and gaps in the field, the paper aims to advance academic discussion and lay a foundation for future research in sustainability management.},
